          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "Unleashed already removes the region locks, so most users only need to add their frequency to the user settings file.\n\n**Add a custom frequency**\n1. On the SD card, go to `subghz/assets/` and rename `setting_user.example` to `setting_user`.\n2. Add your frequency in Hz, for example `Frequency: 928000000`. For the hopper, use `Hopper_frequency: …`.\n3. Reboot the Flipper. The frequency then shows up in Sub-GHz Read and Send.\n\nThe CC1101 radio only covers roughly 300–348, 387–464 and 779–928 MHz. Anything outside those bands won't work without the second unlock below.\n\n**Beyond hardware spec (rarely needed)**\n- Edit `subghz/assets/dangerous_settings` and change `false` to `true`.\n- **This can physically damage the radio.** It is a separate switch from the region unlock.\n\n**Legal note:** Unleashed removes the guardrails but not the law. Which frequencies and power levels you may transmit on depends on your jurisdiction (FCC, ISED, CE and others), and that responsibility is yours. Only transmit on bands you're licensed or allowed to use.\n\nIf you want, I can pull the exact `setting_user` file format from `references/subghz.md`."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
