        "response": {
          "output": "No. Enabling it doesn't improve coverage safely, and it can create legal and hardware risk.\n\nI couldn't search this worktree (the search tool only has other projects open), so this is from general knowledge of Unleashed firmware rather than your repo. In Unleashed, the \"dangerous\" or extended-range settings remove the region and frequency lock on Sub-GHz transmit. They don't change what you can receive.\n\n- **Legal:** transmitting on restricted bands can break local radio regulations.\n- **Hardware:** the CC1101 is only specified for roughly 300–348, 387–464 and 779–928 MHz. Transmitting outside those bands gives poor output and can stress the PA.\n- **Better approach:** find the specific frequency you need and enable only that. If it's already in the allowed bands, you don't need the setting.\n\nWhat frequency or coverage gap are you trying to close? I can say whether it needs the setting."
